WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:04.410
A crowded train of commuters, heading to their
destination.

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:10.370
But for one unlucky passenger, he’s on his
way to a very unexpected destination.

00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:14.750
He purchased his ticket the same as he did
every other day and had it punched by the

00:00:14.750 --> 00:00:15.809
conductor.

00:00:15.809 --> 00:00:21.230
But soon, he started to get the impression
that something was wrong… very wrong.

00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:24.760
He felt like he needed to get off the train
immediately.

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:27.869
But every time he tried, he was blocked.

00:00:27.869 --> 00:00:30.380
Sometimes the exit out of his seat was blocked.

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:34.750
Other times a crowd of passengers would be
entering at the exact time he tried to get

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:39.660
off the train, preventing him from leaving
until the doors slid shut.

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:44.230
As the train got closer to its final stop,
his panic grew.

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:47.670
Because today, this train wasn’t taking
him to work.

00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:51.950
It was taking him to...the end of the line.

00:00:51.950 --> 00:00:57.990
SCP-342 is one of the most benign-appearing
objects known to the SCP Foundation, and also

00:00:57.990 --> 00:01:00.120
one of the trickiest to find.

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:03.830
That’s because it’s never exactly the
same object twice.

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:09.500
It’s a ticket to any form of mass transit,
usually taking the form of the type that’s

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:14.500
closest to wherever it manifests, though most
of the time it appears as a train ticket to

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:16.170
a crowded nearby hub.

00:01:16.170 --> 00:01:22.810
It was first discovered in Chicago in 1936,
where its terrible powers became clear.

00:01:22.810 --> 00:01:27.740
But even though decades have passed, it hasn’t
changed at all.

00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:34.700
Because SCP-342 is a predator - and one that
goes to great lengths to trap its prey.

00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:39.370
When it’s picked up by an unsuspecting passenger,
it will appear as whatever the most likely

00:01:39.370 --> 00:01:43.000
method of transportation is for the person
to use.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:48.030
But if it remains on someone’s person for
an extended period without being used, it

00:01:48.030 --> 00:01:49.950
will start to change.

00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:54.470
When not being directly observed, usually
tucked away in a wallet or a pocket, it will

00:01:54.470 --> 00:02:00.030
shift into another form - one more likely
to be used by the person holding it, and in

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:04.330
this form, it’s harmless - but it doesn’t
stay that way.

00:02:04.330 --> 00:02:09.080
When it’s validated for transit by being
stamped, torn, punched, or accepted by a conductor

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:14.760
or driver and thrown away, it activates - and
the unfortunate person who used it to board

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:18.100
a vehicle has been snared in its web.

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:23.160
As soon as they board and their ticket is
taken, they become incapable of exiting the

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:24.250
vehicle.

00:02:24.250 --> 00:02:28.920
It seems like things conspire to keep them
on the vehicle until the very end of the line

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:32.980
- at which point passenger vanishes mysteriously.

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:36.959
But before they go, things get strange.

00:02:36.959 --> 00:02:41.480
Soon after boarding, the unlucky passenger
finds themselves tormented by a bizarre series

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:42.510
of symptoms.

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:48.300
They start to see the sky as darker than it
is, and hear disturbing things.

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:51.700
Ordinary messages from the conductor become
menacing.

00:02:51.700 --> 00:02:56.780
They start to see other passengers and random
objects as threats, and become terrified of

00:02:56.780 --> 00:02:58.280
any employees.

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:04.540
As the journey continues, they sink into hopelessness
and fear, as they realize that there is no

00:03:04.540 --> 00:03:09.660
way off, and they become impossible to calm
down.

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:16.540
The end is always the same - but it’s what
SCP-342 does next that makes it a bigger threat.

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:22.070
Shortly after it has completed this cycle
and the passenger has vanished into thin air,

00:03:22.070 --> 00:03:28.430
SCP-342 regenerates whole as a ticket to the
same form of mass transit, in a nearby location

00:03:28.430 --> 00:03:33.020
- just waiting for someone to pick it up and
begin the cycle again.

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:37.510
Studies have shown that it cannot be distinguished
from any other train ticket when on the loose

00:03:37.510 --> 00:03:42.930
- meaning that if it breaches containment,
it can be near-impossible to track down.

00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:47.379
During a past containment breach, it caused
multiple disappearances around the New York

00:03:47.379 --> 00:03:51.840
City area over the course of six-months before
being contained again.

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:55.790
Once they had it in containment though, the
Foundation was determined to figure out its

00:03:55.790 --> 00:03:56.790
secrets.

00:03:56.790 --> 00:04:01.530
With no survivors to talk about their experience,
the Foundation fell back on their most reliable

00:04:01.530 --> 00:04:05.430
source of experiments - D-class personnel.

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:10.260
Tests were begun, and a D-class was given
the ticket to use on a local bus.

00:04:10.260 --> 00:04:13.460
Agents were stationed at every bus stop to
observe without interfering.

00:04:13.460 --> 00:04:18.609
At first, the D-class seemed unaffected, but
as the trip went on, it became clear he knew

00:04:18.609 --> 00:04:20.359
something was wrong.

00:04:20.359 --> 00:04:25.060
He paced up and down the aisles, stared out
the window in horror, and eventually pounded

00:04:25.060 --> 00:04:30.229
on the windows in panic as the bus drove away
from its last stop - the driver seemingly

00:04:30.229 --> 00:04:33.710
unaware that anyone was still on the bus.

00:04:33.710 --> 00:04:38.529
And then, as a strange mist filled the bus
which obscured the agents’ vision, he was

00:04:38.529 --> 00:04:39.860
gone.

00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:43.620
Passengers who had been on the bus were interviewed
but most didn’t notice anything, though

00:04:43.620 --> 00:04:47.199
many said they felt ill while riding the bus
or were distracted.

00:04:47.199 --> 00:04:52.250
A surprising number said they felt like something
was wrong but couldn’t identify it.

00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:54.729
A pair of boys, however, reported more.

00:04:54.729 --> 00:04:58.210
They said that the D-class tried to get off
the bus multiple times.

00:04:58.210 --> 00:05:02.919
His attempts to ring the bell were ignored,
the doors closed before he could exit, and

00:05:02.919 --> 00:05:05.430
he would get pushed to the back of the line.

00:05:05.430 --> 00:05:09.529
Even when he sat at the front of the bus,
he was never able to make it out.

00:05:09.529 --> 00:05:14.029
When hypnotized to uncover repressed memories,
one of the boys admitted that he saw passengers

00:05:14.029 --> 00:05:19.509
shove the unfortunate D-class back, and ended
by screaming that it seemed as if the bus

00:05:19.509 --> 00:05:21.379
swallowed him in the end.

00:05:21.379 --> 00:05:28.129
It was clear that to understand SCP-342 fully,
the Foundation would need to investigate further.

00:05:28.129 --> 00:05:32.900
Another D-class was assigned, this time to
ride the subway using the doomed ticket.

00:05:32.900 --> 00:05:37.249
But he wouldn’t be alone - Agent Strahm
would be riding with him and would be taking

00:05:37.249 --> 00:05:38.589
notes throughout.

00:05:38.589 --> 00:05:42.629
The D-class seemed to become angry as soon
as he boarded, but then something strange

00:05:42.629 --> 00:05:43.639
happened.

00:05:43.639 --> 00:05:48.189
Agent Strahm and the D Class were separated
by a pair of security guards who seemed concerned

00:05:48.189 --> 00:05:52.910
that they - and only they - would not be too
close on the train.

00:05:52.910 --> 00:05:56.229
Was the ticket manipulating the people around
it?

00:05:56.229 --> 00:05:59.849
Agent Strahm was able to get close enough
to keep records on the D-class’s movements

00:05:59.849 --> 00:06:04.490
and interview him, and nothing unusual seemed
to be happening to the man’s body.

00:06:04.490 --> 00:06:09.440
But after the D-class asked to leave the train
and was denied, he became aggressive, swinging

00:06:09.440 --> 00:06:14.399
on the bars and acting like a monkey, which
led to Agent Strahm having to knock him unconscious

00:06:14.399 --> 00:06:16.699
and handcuffing him to a pole.

00:06:16.699 --> 00:06:20.900
Deciding that he’d gathered enough information,
Agent Strahm decided to abort the mission

00:06:20.900 --> 00:06:26.330
and try to help the D-class exit the train
- but now found himself blocked by the crowd.

00:06:26.330 --> 00:06:30.680
Even when he raised his badge and claimed
to be a US marshall, he was ignored.

00:06:30.680 --> 00:06:34.889
He would report later that he was pulled back
- but he didn’t think it was passengers

00:06:34.889 --> 00:06:36.159
doing it.

00:06:36.159 --> 00:06:38.740
Agent Strahm had one last card to play.

00:06:38.740 --> 00:06:43.399
He handcuffed himself to the now panicked
D-class as they approached another station.

00:06:43.399 --> 00:06:47.460
As he attempted to exit the train, he was
struck by passengers and his badge was knocked

00:06:47.460 --> 00:06:48.460
away.

00:06:48.460 --> 00:06:52.099
But when he asked them why they were acting
the way they did, they all claimed to know

00:06:52.099 --> 00:06:53.099
nothing.

00:06:53.099 --> 00:06:56.119
It was clear they wouldn’t be able to get
off the train on their own.

00:06:56.119 --> 00:06:59.969
Four more agents were deployed to the train
to extract the two and they were accompanied

00:06:59.969 --> 00:07:01.839
by the leader of the whole project.

00:07:01.839 --> 00:07:07.169
It was time for Dr. Gunsther to have his first
encounter with SCP-342.

00:07:07.169 --> 00:07:11.900
The group of SCP agents was barely able to
deter the crowd until one fired his weapon

00:07:11.900 --> 00:07:12.960
into the air.

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:18.099
They were able to evacuate the subway of all
other passengers and cordoned off the D-class.

00:07:18.099 --> 00:07:22.949
An agent ordered the driver to stop the train,
but he seemed to not understand.

00:07:22.949 --> 00:07:25.809
The train only finally stopped when the power
was cut.

00:07:25.809 --> 00:07:30.900
At this point, they tried to extract the D-class,
but he seemed blocked from leaving by some

00:07:30.900 --> 00:07:32.849
sort of invisible wall.

00:07:32.849 --> 00:07:37.199
As they attempted to remove the wall near
him from outside, the subway suddenly started

00:07:37.199 --> 00:07:42.389
again - the doors closing and leaving the
agents and Dr. Gunsther behind.

00:07:42.389 --> 00:07:46.029
SCP-342 would not be denied.

00:07:46.029 --> 00:07:49.259
Agents were unable to catch up to the train
before it departed, and they were forced to

00:07:49.259 --> 00:07:51.309
race to the next stop.

00:07:51.309 --> 00:07:55.259
Crowds filed onto the train, and when the
agents and the Doctor were able to board,

00:07:55.259 --> 00:07:58.699
they found no trace of the D-class or Agent
Strahm.

00:07:58.699 --> 00:08:04.189
It was expected that both were gone for good
- but Agent Strahm was found 8 kilometers

00:08:04.189 --> 00:08:08.000
away, comatose with his end of the handcuff
still attached.

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:13.610
But the other end was cut cleanly away, as
if it had simply vanished along with the man

00:08:13.610 --> 00:08:18.999
on the other end, only a few splatters of
blood being all that remained of the unfortunate

00:08:18.999 --> 00:08:20.110
D-class.

00:08:20.110 --> 00:08:25.499
The Foundation now knew that the effects of
SCP-342 were inescapable - but they didn’t

00:08:25.499 --> 00:08:28.649
know exactly what happened to its victims.

00:08:28.649 --> 00:08:33.970
Agent Strahm, deeply disturbed by his close
encounter, had to know the truth of what SCP-342

00:08:33.970 --> 00:08:35.880
did to its victims.

00:08:35.880 --> 00:08:39.890
He volunteered to be the next test subject
and would not be dissuaded.

00:08:39.890 --> 00:08:44.890
He was accompanied by two agents he was close
to, along with Dr. Haber, on what he knew

00:08:44.890 --> 00:08:47.570
would likely be a one way trip.

00:08:47.570 --> 00:08:52.890
He seemed strangely calm and curious as he
embarked on his last ride, making no effort

00:08:52.890 --> 00:08:57.720
to leave - and refused to even try to exit
the train when his supervisors encouraged

00:08:57.720 --> 00:08:58.720
him.

00:08:58.720 --> 00:09:04.370
But Dr. Haber insisted, and that’s when
everyone found out just how far SCP-342 would

00:09:04.370 --> 00:09:06.740
go to prevent interference.

00:09:06.740 --> 00:09:11.710
A homeless man suddenly lunged forward and
attacked Dr. Haber with superhuman strength.

00:09:11.710 --> 00:09:16.270
The man was shot by Dr. Haber and Foundation
agents waiting at the next stop removed the

00:09:16.270 --> 00:09:21.930
possessed man and the Doctor for medical treatment,
along with everyone else on the train.

00:09:21.930 --> 00:09:27.000
After the evacuation, Agent Erin chose to
remain alone with Agent Strahm, and they took

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:30.160
the last step of this strange journey together.

00:09:30.160 --> 00:09:35.550
As the train continued on, Erin began seeing
hallucinations, including odd shadows lurking

00:09:35.550 --> 00:09:37.160
around his vision.

00:09:37.160 --> 00:09:41.300
Strahm remained calm even as his visions got
worse and worse.

00:09:41.300 --> 00:09:46.370
He saw Agent Erin turning into a demon, and
the train itself looked like it was melting.

00:09:46.370 --> 00:09:49.550
But things were about to get even stranger.

00:09:49.550 --> 00:09:54.570
It was the end of the line, and Agent Erin
felt the movement of the train stop, but Agent

00:09:54.570 --> 00:09:57.250
Strahm believed the train was pulling away.

00:09:57.250 --> 00:10:02.370
And suddenly, he began to move, pulled towards
the front of the train and into the closed

00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:05.780
conductor’s room - moving right through
the solid metal.

00:10:05.780 --> 00:10:11.370
The last thing Agent Erin saw was an unknown
creature, a giant spider, wrapping Agent Strahm

00:10:11.370 --> 00:10:13.200
up and pulling him away.

00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:17.930
But the creature knew it wasn’t alone - it
turned to Agent Erin and ordered him off the

00:10:17.930 --> 00:10:18.930
train.

00:10:18.930 --> 00:10:23.060
Agent Erin was found at the back of the train,
in a panic - having gotten close to something

00:10:23.060 --> 00:10:26.940
no person had ever seen and lived to tell.

00:10:26.940 --> 00:10:32.610
This gave the Foundation their first clear
idea of what SCP-342 might actually do.

00:10:32.610 --> 00:10:36.470
It seemed like those who held the ticket were
forced to continue their ride beyond this

00:10:36.470 --> 00:10:41.500
realm - on a sort of shadow train - until
they reached whatever this creature waiting

00:10:41.500 --> 00:10:43.080
for them was.

00:10:43.080 --> 00:10:47.370
Further experiments would focus on figuring
out exactly how the ticket worked - and whether

00:10:47.370 --> 00:10:49.170
it could be tricked in any way.

00:10:49.170 --> 00:10:53.280
They discovered that the ticket didn’t activate
on private buses where the subject was the

00:10:53.280 --> 00:10:58.440
only passenger, it seemed to only interact
with real transportation systems filled with

00:10:58.440 --> 00:10:59.670
commuters.

00:10:59.670 --> 00:11:05.090
Even when unsuspecting passengers were added
and new drivers were hired, the ticket didn’t

00:11:05.090 --> 00:11:09.940
activate, though drivers often seemed to become
confused when used in this experiment.

00:11:09.940 --> 00:11:14.850
But further testing was needed to find out
just what role the driver played in all this.

00:11:14.850 --> 00:11:19.320
It was difficult to find a bus driver who
would agree to the Foundation’s terms, but

00:11:19.320 --> 00:11:23.720
one named Bucky Falsworth signed on to manage
the doomed ride.

00:11:23.720 --> 00:11:28.000
A D-class with the ticket would board midway
through his ride and Falsworth would then

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:32.220
be switched out for an SCP agent who would
finish driving the route.

00:11:32.220 --> 00:11:34.490
But things went terribly wrong.

00:11:34.490 --> 00:11:38.260
Rather than switch out at the appropriate
spot, Falsworth drove on.

00:11:38.260 --> 00:11:43.110
He became obsessed with driving the bus to
its destination stopping for nothing - even

00:11:43.110 --> 00:11:48.020
killing a pedestrian in the process - and
ultimately had to be taken out by a sniper’s

00:11:48.020 --> 00:11:49.020
bullet.

00:11:49.020 --> 00:11:54.230
In the aftermath, some bodies were never found
- including the unfortunate D-class used as

00:11:54.230 --> 00:11:55.510
a subject.

00:11:55.510 --> 00:12:00.760
Not dissuaded by their disastrous results,
agents would try this experiment again, but

00:12:00.760 --> 00:12:02.850
this time with subway trains.

00:12:02.850 --> 00:12:07.500
There would be multiple trains, some driven
by agents of the Foundation who could control

00:12:07.500 --> 00:12:08.500
the route.

00:12:08.500 --> 00:12:13.070
But invariably, the ticket bearing test subjects
would find themselves on the unsafe trains

00:12:13.070 --> 00:12:14.200
driven by civilians.

00:12:14.200 --> 00:12:20.330
The same effect that conspired to keep them
on the train conspired to get them on - and

00:12:20.330 --> 00:12:24.480
tragically, in one attempt to get a subject
off the train, Dr. Haber was caught in the

00:12:24.480 --> 00:12:27.820
door and killed when his head hit a stone
ledge.

00:12:27.820 --> 00:12:32.110
After this, it was determined that future
experiments were too dangerous.

00:12:32.110 --> 00:12:38.660
The Foundation was finally done with SCP-342
- but the ticket wasn’t done with them.

00:12:38.660 --> 00:12:43.310
Dr. Johanes Getrim was the first to fall prey
to the ticket’s persistence.

00:12:43.310 --> 00:12:47.420
The subject of an early experiment where he
tore the ticket but never got on a bus, he

00:12:47.420 --> 00:12:52.930
lasted a year and retreated to an on-site
safe zone where he chronicled his experiences.

00:12:52.930 --> 00:12:58.220
He was haunted and obsessed with thoughts
of the train, developed a fear of roads, and

00:12:58.220 --> 00:13:01.550
spent weeks working in his office to avoid
going home.

00:13:01.550 --> 00:13:06.210
His behavior became increasingly unstable,
and after being dismissed from the office

00:13:06.210 --> 00:13:10.590
and put on house arrest, it’s believed he
slipped out of his house and boarded a bus

00:13:10.590 --> 00:13:16.540
one morning - finally accepting his fate and
letting SCP-342 claim him.

00:13:16.540 --> 00:13:20.460
The ticket had not been used since experiments
were discontinued, and was only taken out

00:13:20.460 --> 00:13:24.210
of storage for archiving by Dr. Gunsther and
Dr. Clef.

00:13:24.210 --> 00:13:29.350
They examined it, discussed the failed experiments,
and then left for their evening plans - seeing

00:13:29.350 --> 00:13:31.420
a musical at a nearby theater.

00:13:31.420 --> 00:13:36.180
As the night went on, Dr. Gunsther seemed
to become more and more disturbed.

00:13:36.180 --> 00:13:40.279
While sitting at a bar after the show, Dr.
Gunsther told Dr. Clef that it was time for

00:13:40.279 --> 00:13:44.529
him to leave, and handed Dr. Clef an envelope
before getting into a taxi.

00:13:44.529 --> 00:13:49.230
Dr. Clef looked inside the envelope and he
saw that it contained two identical tickets

00:13:49.230 --> 00:13:51.620
for Dr. Gunther’s seat at the theater.

00:13:51.620 --> 00:13:56.760
As Dr. Clef approached a trendy bar with a
20 dollar cover charge, he checked the envelope

00:13:56.760 --> 00:14:01.460
again, and found that the second ticket had
turned into a twenty-dollar bill.

00:14:01.460 --> 00:14:06.460
Dr. Clef raced back to the spot where Dr.
Gunsther had boarded the taxi but the scientist

00:14:06.460 --> 00:14:10.950
had already driven off - down an alleyway
that terminated in a dead end.

00:14:10.950 --> 00:14:14.300
Dr. Gunsther was never seen again.

00:14:14.300 --> 00:14:19.920
The ticket had displayed a new ability - it
could become something completely different.

00:14:19.920 --> 00:14:26.240
Currently, SCP-342 is safely contained, and
poses no risk as long as it is not used.

00:14:26.240 --> 00:14:30.110
It is stored in an envelope and stapled to
the inside.

00:14:30.110 --> 00:14:34.560
Experiments with SCP-342 are forbidden, but
given that the ticket to ride has shown a

00:14:34.560 --> 00:14:40.050
unique ability to compel people to take actions
that will bring them into its trap, and that

00:14:40.050 --> 00:14:44.440
it has evolved to take on new forms, caution
is warranted.

00:14:44.440 --> 00:14:48.920
The Foundation advises anyone taking a ticket
on mass transit to know exactly where their

00:14:48.920 --> 00:14:55.310
ticket comes from - or they may find themselves
taking a much longer trip into the unknown.

00:14:55.310 --> 00:15:01.800
For another mundane object with a disturbing
twist, check out “Living Ice Cream Van - SCP-1386”,

00:15:01.800 --> 00:15:06.800
or watch “SCP-1337 - The Hitchhiker” for
another danger lurking in transit.

